<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings flat, most stay in NWE.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings flat, most stay in NWE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal totalled 799,265 tonnes in the week to November 26, virtually unchanged from 797,323 tonnes the previous week, the Shetland Islands Council Marine Operations Department said.</p>
<p>The shipments were mostly destined for northwest Europe and Britain as U.S. sailings dropped off sharply.</p>
